> This resource takes **no input**. The Dynatrace GCP Principal is a tenant-wide singleton that is provisioned by Dynatrace; this resource triggers its creation (if it does not exist yet), waits until it becomes available, and returns it. Creating the resource when a principal already exists is a no-op that simply reads the existing one.

> <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`update`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Update`" pulumi-lang-go="`update`" pulumi-lang-python="`update`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`update`" pulumi-lang-java="`update`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`update`">`update`</span> and <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`delete`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Delete`" pulumi-lang-go="`delete`" pulumi-lang-python="`delete`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`delete`" pulumi-lang-java="`delete`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`delete`">`delete`</span> are no-ops. Because the principal is a Dynatrace-managed singleton, `terraform destroy` removes the resource from state but leaves the principal in place.

> This resource requires the API token scopes **Read settings** (`settings.read`) and **Write settings** (`settings.write`), and the OAuth scopes **Read settings** (`settings:objects:read`) and **Write settings** (`settings:objects:write`).

